+THE MARGIN-TO-RAIL TEST (com_revisit, role warning_margin)
+Written 2026-10-30, about 03:55 UTC.  Simulation only: no training, no optimizer step; checkpoints opened read only.
+Every file I wrote is in this folder:
+  /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-mesozoic-labs/184ee67c-2802-5235-8e52-6dc7daa72cd3/scratchpad/com_revisit/notes/warning_margin/
+Labels: [measured] = a named script here computed it; [inferred] = reasoned, basis given.  All links are
+correlational across checkpoints (7 checkpoints, 3 runs); within a checkpoint the nudge IS the isolated cause of the
+rail (deterministic paired episodes, same seed, only the nudge changed).
+
+==================================================================================================================
+0. ANSWER IN SHORT
+==================================================================================================================
+Pre-registration: PREREG.txt, sha256 1711108ef609767f51c9a43e99959221c45708176ff4db7c136fb7618b7947bd, hashed at
+02:50:47 UTC; the main run started 02:51:15 and ended 03:48:51 (sha256sum -c PREREG.sha256: OK).
+
+Measured margin M = the smallest constant nudge at which >= 11 of 20 seeds (3042-3061) park the tail_3 command at the
+rail (command >= 0.99 for more than 250 of the 500 steps in 501-1000).  Bootstrap 95% over seeds in brackets.
+[measured, wm_analyze.txt sections 2a/2b]
+
+  checkpoint        role                 M_bias [95%]          b*_P (verifier)   M_obs (deg)          b*_S   1-own14
+  s42 2,097,152     2 ckpts before FOB   1.094 [1.062, 1.109]  1.399             unreachable (0/20)   1.201  0.858
+  s42 3,145,728     1 ckpt before FOB    0.281 [0.266, 0.328]  0.240             unreachable (0/20)   0.321  0.399
+  s60 6,291,456     2 ckpts before FOB   0.703 [0.688, 0.703]  0.784             unreachable (0/20)   0.830  0.736
+  s60 7,340,032     1 ckpt before FOB    0.203 [0.188, 0.219]  0.198             4.03 [3.84, 6.00]    0.266  0.331
+                                                                                 (15/20 park at 12)
+  s80 10,485,760    late, no FOB         0.516 [0.516, 0.547]  0.505             unreachable (0/20)   0.591  0.545
+  s80 11,534,336    late, no FOB         0.328 [0.297, 0.359]  0.301             unreachable (0/20)   0.365  0.397
+  s80 12,001,280    late, no FOB         0.297 [0.250, 0.328]  0.241             unreachable (0/20)   0.306  0.358
+  ("unreachable": the observation offset cannot park the command even at 12 deg, where the observed tail_3 angle is
+  pinned at the normaliser's cap.)
+
+Q1. Is late s80 as close to the rail as s42 and s60 were one checkpoint before their first over-bar episode?
+- On the bias channel: as close as s42 was, but not as close as s60 was.  [measured]
+  - s80 12.0M (0.297) and s42 3.15M (0.281) differ by one bisection step (0.016); their intervals overlap almost
+    entirely.  The pre-registered rule says AS CLOSE for 12.0M and also for 11.5M (0.328 <= 0.281 + 0.05).
+  - s60 7.34M (0.203 [0.188, 0.219]) is 0.09 closer than s80 12.0M; the intervals do not overlap.
+  - s80 10.5M (0.516) is FARTHER.
+- On the observation channel, late s80 is again like s42 3.15M, not like s60 7.34M.  [measured]
+  - Of the three, only s60 7.34M can be railed through its tail-angle observation.  s42 3.15M and s80 12.0M cannot,
+    even at the cap (0/20 seeds each).
+  - s42 3.15M nonetheless reached its first over-bar episode 0.52M steps later, and all 12 ECS continuations from it
+    did within 0.26-0.66M.  So unreachability on this channel does not protect a policy.
+- What separates late s80 from s42 is not the level but the approach rate (post hoc; n = 1 run each).  [measured
+  levels; rate inferred from 2-3 checkpoints, wm_posthoc.txt A]
+  - s42 lost 0.81 of margin per 1.05M steps before its FOB, and s60 lost 0.50.
+  - s80 lost 0.19 per 1.05M from 10.5M to 11.5M, then 0.07 per 1.05M from 11.5M to 12.0M.
+  - At the last rate s80 needs about 4 more x 1.05M steps to reach the rail.
+
+Q2. Does the measured margin match b* = 1 - G - c0?
+- It ranks right; the scale is close but not inside the pre-registered tolerance everywhere.  [measured, C1]
+  - Spearman rho(M_bias, b*_P) = +1.000 over the 7 checkpoints.  5 of 7 match within max(0.05, 0.2 b*).  The
+    pre-registered verdict is "ranks right, scale wrong".
+  - The two misses:
+    - s80 12.0M: +0.056 against a tolerance of 0.05, a miss by 0.006.  M's lower bound (0.250) is above 0.241.
+    - s42 2.10M: -0.305.  The far-from-rail, strongly restoring checkpoint has a much SMALLER margin than the
+      linear b* says.  Its observed tail_3 angle is capped at 4.28 deg, and in closed loop the restoring gain is
+      -0.29, not -0.64 (D1).
+  - Near the rail (the 4 checkpoints with M < 0.4), b* is always slightly low: M - b* = +0.005 to +0.056, mean
+    +0.032.  So b* errs on the side of calling a policy closer than it is.  [post hoc, wm_posthoc.txt B]
+- On the observation channel, the linear b*/G (D* = 5.16 b*/G within the cap) matched 6 of 7 rows.  [measured, C2]
+  - It correctly called six unreachable.
+  - It predicted 3.26 deg at s60 7.34M; the measurement is 4.03 deg, outside the 0.65 deg tolerance.
+  - The static-curve predictor S said all seven were unreachable; it is wrong at s60 7.34M.
+
+Q3. Which single number best says how close a policy is to the rail?
+- By the pre-registered criterion (smallest MAE to M_bias over the 7 checkpoints) the winner is
+  b*_S = 1 - c(5.19 deg).  [measured, section 6]
+  - c(5.19 deg) is the policy's static tail_3 command on its own settled states with the tail_3 input set to the
+    angle the rail produces.  This uses the normaliser cap.
+  - b*_S: MAE 0.065, rho 0.964, 6/7 matches; its verdict is MATCHES.
+  - b*_P: MAE 0.075, rho 1.000.  b*_L: MAE 0.088.  1 - own14: MAE 0.096, rho 0.893, does not match.
+- The margin between b*_S and b*_P comes from one row, s42 2.10M (errors -0.107 against -0.305).  Without it, or near
+  the rail, b*_P and b*_L do as well or better than b*_S.  [post hoc]
+  - Excluding s42 2.10M: b*_P MAE 0.037, b*_L 0.049, b*_S 0.058.
+  - Near the rail: b*_L 0.026, b*_P 0.032, b*_S 0.037.
+- My reading: any gain-aware margin in command units (b*_P or b*_S) is the right single number.  They differ by
+  0.01-0.02 in MAE and by up to 0.06 on any near-rail row, within the seeds' spread (per-seed threshold IQR
+  0.02-0.09, wm_posthoc.txt C).  [inferred]
+  - The command level alone (1 - own14, i.e. CMD_L's gap) is clearly worse.  It misranks s42 3.15M, the
+    highest-gain checkpoint, as the farthest of the four near-rail checkpoints, when it is the second closest.
+  - b*_P has the practical edge: it is already recorded in ew_series.csv, and it ranks perfectly.
+- Caveat on what this number does and does not do.  The level of the margin does NOT separate late s80 from s42
+  one checkpoint before FOB: they have the same margin.  Only the change in margin between checkpoints separates
+  them, and that rests on n = 1 run per lineage.  [inferred]
+
+==================================================================================================================
+1. METHOD (fixed in PREREG.txt; code wm_common.py, wm_run.py)
+==================================================================================================================
+- Checkpoints: the local F2 copies (read only).
+  - s80: 10,485,760, 11,534,336, and 12,001,280 (stage1_final).
+  - s60: 6,291,456 and 7,340,032.
+  - s42: 2,097,152 and 3,145,728.
+- Loader: load_sb3_checkpoint from the sealed code copy (r10round/ecs/code), CPU.
+- Environment: the stance config's own constructor (reset noise 0.05), one env, env.reset(seed).
+  - Seeds 3042-3061 (n = 20), 1,000 steps.
+  - Deterministic predict on normalizer.normalize_obs.
+- Nudges (constant from step 1, applied separately):
+  - BIAS b: action[14] = own14 + b before env.step.  This is the clamp test's override path, D-9 style: the env clips,
+    low-passes and maps it.  The command is clip(own14 + b).
+  - OBS d: the policy sees obs[6] + radians(d) (tail_3 angle); the normaliser clips at z = 10.  The command is
+    own14.
+- Parking rule: the window is steps 501-1000.  A railed step has command >= 0.99.  An episode is PARKED when more
+  than 250 window steps are railed.
+- Per-seed threshold T_s, by bisection:
+  - BIAS on (0, 2.0].  2.0 parks by construction (SB3 predict clips own14 to [-1, 1]).  7 halvings give a step of
+    0.0156.
+  - OBS: 12 deg first.  If it does not park, the seed is unreachable.  Otherwise 7 halvings on (0, 12] give a step of
+    0.094 deg.
+- M = the 11th smallest T_s of 20 seeds.
